<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI11-QA5-ATM-QA-002-DELETION-GATE-TEST>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI11-QA5-ATM-QA-002-DELETION-GATE-TEST" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "Missing deletion-gate AST/dependency scan test" ;
  triage:description "AI.11 sprint doc requires a deletion-gate AST/dependency scan test verifying deleted UDS-transport code paths cannot be silently reintroduced. This test was never implemented. Should follow the same style as existing AST-based tests in crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "QA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:resolution "Real closing fix is commit bb20fd9a on feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation (PR #607): a syn-AST + Cargo-dependency-based deletion-gate test replacing the earlier, weaker lexical test from 472a9225. Scans shared/Windows transport surfaces including atm-core/protocol.rs, preserves the macOS/Linux Unix-only UDS implementation unchanged. `just lint` and `just test` both passed on bb20fd9a. PR comment: https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/607#issuecomment-5050727890." ;
  triage:notes "DISPUTED, not a confirmed false closure -- QA-6's absence claim appears to be a stale-worktree artifact, not an actual missing test. quality-mgr's QA-6 pass (PR #607 comment https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/607#issuecomment-5050680007) reported, via full-file read + workspace-wide grep of 'the commit under review, 472a9225', zero matches for named_pipe/AF_UNIX/deletion_gate/etc. and a 764-line file. Direct re-verification (team-lead, 2026-07-22) of commit 472a9225 itself (git show 472a9225:crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs) shows the commit DOES add the required test: const AI11_RETIRED_WINDOWS_TRANSPORT_SYMBOLS list plus fn ai11_deletion_gate_preserves_windows_loopback_transport_boundary() and fn ai11_deletion_gate_detector_rejects_retired_windows_transport_fixture(), 859 lines total, covering all six sprint-doc Required-Tests-table items (pipe, AF_UNIX, generic frame codec, duplicate router, non-loopback bind, adapter storage/nudge calls). PR #607's headRefOid is confirmed 472a9225 via `gh pr view 607`. Critically: the local worktree at feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation was found (before a fresh `git pull`) sitting one commit BEHIND origin, at 8a7ea589 (763 lines, no deletion-gate test) -- an exact byte-for-byte match to QA-6's reported '764 lines' / zero-match state. This strongly suggests QA-6's reviewer subagents read that same un-pulled local worktree rather than the actual commit 472a9225 content, i.e. a worktree-fetch hygiene bug in the QA pipeline, not a false-closure by the triage record. Status was set to 'disputed' pending: (1) re-running QA-6 against a freshly-pulled worktree, (2) confirming with quality-mgr which path/commit its subagents actually read. UPDATE (team-lead, 2026-07-22, post-dispute): cwin (dev) subsequently pushed commit bb20fd9a on top of 472a9225, replacing the earlier lexical/grep-based test with a stronger syn-AST-parsed + Cargo-dependency-graph deletion gate covering shared/Windows transport surfaces including atm-core/protocol.rs, while leaving the macOS/Linux Unix-only UDS implementation untouched. `just lint` and `just test` reported passing by cwin; see PR #607 comment https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/607#issuecomment-5050727890. This supersedes the disputed-verification question entirely: regardless of whether QA-6 read a stale worktree for 472a9225, bb20fd9a is a materially stronger, freshly-pushed gate that satisfies the sprint-doc requirement on its own merits. Status moved from 'disputed' to 'fixed' on this basis. QA-7 is dispatched to re-verify bb20fd9a on a freshly-pulled worktree (to avoid repeating QA-6's stale-worktree failure mode) plus normal full-scope QA-7 review per the AI.11 sprint doc." ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s11/8a7ea589> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s11/8a7ea589> ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI11-QA5-ATM-QA-002-DELETION-GATE-TEST>
  triage:assignedTo "cwin" ;
  triage:dispatchChannel "direct-paste-non-atm" ;
  triage:notes "OWNERSHIP BACKFILL (team-lead, 2026-07-22): this record was closed as 'fixed' citing commit bb20fd9a (see triage:resolution above) before the assignedTo/dispatchChannel ownership-tracking convention existed, so those fields were absent until this backfill. cwin (dev) closed this finding via commit bb20fd9a on feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation (PR #607): a syn-AST + Cargo-dependency-graph deletion-gate test replacing the earlier lexical/grep-based test. cwin has no ATM identity, so this work was dispatched and reported by direct-paste outside the ATM channel and left no ATM message trail on his side. This backfill is retroactive-only -- triage:status, triage:resolution, and the existing triage:notes narrative above are unchanged; only the ownership/dispatch-channel audit fields are being added, consistent with the same convention already applied to the AI11-QA7 fast-follow batch (AI11-QA7-ATM-QA-201-ENVELOPE-CODEC-COVERAGE, AI11-QA7-ARCH-001-HARDCODED-ALLOWLIST, AI11-QA7-ARCH-002-TAUTOLOGICAL-DUPLICATE-CHECK)." .

